  "observations": [
    "Host register fixtures exercise independent MMIO and PCI RX/TX queue handles. PCI queue notification offsets differ and unrelated notification slots remain untouched.",
    "Tests require failed configuration to preserve the output handle, reject a different transport owner and invalidate handles on a status reset, including after a fresh queue bind.",
    "The single-queue block wrapper passed the full Spark gate and actual Intel guest write/fsync/read-only cold-boot verification.",
    "No Intel qualification QEMU remained after completion."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The NIC driver has not adopted this API yet. Simultaneous hardware RX/TX queues and PCI NIC traffic are not qualified.",
    "Callers serialize register accesses and discard queue handles when rebinding the transport. Resetting status is not DMA revocation or resource reclamation.",
    "Canonical integration, Debian, GUI and v0.4 release remain incomplete."
  ]
